From 53c1f90a6721a3edf0efccfbd5f49df5ee076eb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tong_1001 <sxt1001@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:42:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix uninitialized memory read in string_to_ascii_hex

string_to_ascii_hex() uses its caller-supplied ascii_string buffer as
both input and output: it calls strlen(ascii_string) and strncat() on
it without first ensuring it is a well-formed empty string. Its sole
caller report_power_off_result_to_bmc() passed a stack-allocated,
uninitialized buffer (power_off_res_hex_str), so strlen() read
indeterminate stack memory until it happened to find a NUL byte,
causing an out-of-bounds / uninitialized-memory read (undefined
behavior).

Fix the issue at the call site by initializing power_off_res_hex_str
to {0} at declaration, guaranteeing the buffer handed to
string_to_ascii_hex() is already a well-formed empty string regardless
of how the callee uses it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sentryPlugins/sentry_msg_monitor/bmc_log_lib.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sentryPlugins/sentry_msg_monitor/bmc_log_lib.c b/src/sentryPlugins/sentry_msg_monitor/bmc_log_lib.c
index fdf95f924904..57b43dc8fe79 100644
--- a/src/sentryPlugins/sentry_msg_monitor/bmc_log_lib.c
+++ b/src/sentryPlugins/sentry_msg_monitor/bmc_log_lib.c
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@ static int report_power_off_result_to_bmc(enum sentry_rmrs_result_type res)
     int ret = 0;
 
     char power_off_res_str[POWER_RESULT_STR_MAX_LEN];
-    char power_off_res_hex_str[POWER_RESULT_STR_MAX_LEN * SINGLE_ASCII_HEX_STR_LEN];
+    char power_off_res_hex_str[POWER_RESULT_STR_MAX_LEN * SINGLE_ASCII_HEX_STR_LEN] = {0};
     char command_ascii_str[IPMITOOL_COMMAND_STR_MAX_LEN];
 
     char *rmrs_result_string = get_rmrs_result_string(res);
